Author: JimmyShi22 <417711026@qq.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 06:13:03 2026 +0800

    Attach the encoded projection table to the gpt2 model commitment
    
    The gpt2 plan now declares the trusted table list of the first migrated
    weight and the model version is two. The commit builds the raw row commitment
    and the encoded table over the same rows; the provider samples the private
    salts and tails, publishes the table leaves in the commit artifact, and writes
    the private randomness to the artifact with its digest. Prove reads the
    private randomness back, decodes it against the trusted parameters, rebuilds
    the same table commitment, and rejects a rebuilt table set that differs from
    the published one. The asset link proof is built over the full anchor record
    list, so a table leaf cannot break asset openings.
    
    The historical context fixture now asserts that the existing model-version
    gate rejects the old-version artifact; the artifact stays on disk. The
    verifier table wiring, the policy regeneration and the consumer relation are
    the next step. No plaintext was removed and every existing asset check
    remains.

